        <div class="details">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <div class="details-content">
              Kneading is a behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing and often carries
              into adulthood as a sign of comfort. Cats may knead to relax, mark a favorite spot
              with scent glands in their paws, or prepare a soft place to rest.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="question-text">What should indoor cats have every day?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <div class="details-content">
              Indoor cats thrive with fresh water, balanced meals, a clean litter box, scratching
              surfaces, climbing areas, and regular interactive play. Rotating toys and adding
              window perches or puzzle feeders can also help prevent boredom.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="question-text">Why do cats suddenly zoom around the house?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="details">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <div class="details-content">
